for a long time and beats by dre were  seen in a negative light mostly due to  the brand really investing into  marketing rather than sound quality and  going into this review we didn't have  high expectations for the beat so low  pro but they ended up surprising us here  at max tech specifically there were four  things that we found surprising about  them and I'll tell you what those are in  just a bit let's start out with a look  in the field of course looks are  subjective but we like them you have six  color options if you want something  sleek and low-key I would go for the  black but if you want to stand out the  red or the blue that we have really pop  they're mostly made of plastic that does  feel more durable than my sonís and  they're not heavy but they do have some  weight to them and do feel nice we have  thick aluminum for the adjustable  headband and also for the hinge which by  the way seems very durable with this  thick aluminum and it also functions to  turn the beats on and off the fact that  they turn on automatically when you  unfold them is really convenient kind of  like how air pods work when you take  them out of the case that also means  that you need to remember to fold them  up to turn them off but once you get  used to this feature having to turn on  other headphones becomes a little bit  annoying we can really see apples  influence here with this feature but  that doesn't stop there we have the h1  chip that does a bunch of things if you  have an iPhone having them close  together will trigger a pop-up making  pairing super easy and once you do the  solos will show up on your other devices  if you have iCloud enabled because  everything is integrated you don't need  a download an app everything is built-in  so holding down on the volume slider in  the control center will allow you swap  between the different modes but more on  that later this deep integration goes  all the way to the charging port where  we unfortunately find a lightning  connector instead of a USB type-c which  we would prefer the solos don't have a  physical headphone port so if you want  to use them wired you will need to buy  Apple's $35 lining two three-and-a-half  millimeter cable where that Jack used to  be we now have a button that lets you  toggle between modes and holding it down  will let you pair to other Bluetooth  devices one thing I want to know is that  Android users can download the beats app  to get information and switch between  modes as well on the right side we have  hidden  cool controls the controls are basically  the same as on the air pod pros pressing  up and down adjust the volume and  pressing down on the center less you  pause skip go back pick up calls and  more depending on how many times you  press holding down will invoke your  assistant but with iOS you could just  say hey Siri instead where it can be  very convenient if your hands are busy  or dirty or whatever the controls work  but we do wish that beats made use of  their right side and the left side to  control tracks instead of using the  center button for everything now let's  get into comfort which completely  depends on the person these are on your  headphones and not everybody is into  that to begin with but then you add the  strong clamping force and that could  make them uncomfortable for people that  have larger heads this clamping force is  needed for a strong seal but thankfully  both the rubber headband and the ear  cups are very comfortable the ear cups  are made from soft memory foam and that  really helps with comfort and provides a  good seal that is needed for the noise  cancellation this also results in the  second surprise and that's how little  sound leak they have even with volume  maxed out to the max where they could be  even too loud for people like me who  love loud music there is almost no sound  that escapes we literally haven't used  any headphones that seal sound in so  well I'm serious about this even if you  max them out and your ears are starting  to hurt from the volume somebody just  next to you can barely hear anything  just a little bit of the high notes and  everything else is sealed out and then  if you drop them to about 85% volume  which is more than enough and sounds  great a person just two feet away can't  hear anything at all now if you don't  like on ear headphones then the solo  pros most likely are not going to change  your mind and over ear headphones are  definitely more comfortable than on your  headphones especially if you use them  for more than say two three or four  hours at a time but I use these for over  two hours maybe about two and a half  hours and it did result and a little bit  of pressure built up but not enough to  make me feel like I have to take them  off like I have felt with other on ears  if you've used other on ear headphones  and don't mind them and you have an  average-sized head these should be  totally fine  next is sound quality which really  surprised me I own the really popular  Sony WH 1000 XM 3s and to me and the  beats actually sound better  previously beats are known for being  very bass heavy and lacking clarity but  possibly thanks to Apple these sounds  the exact opposite basses presence and  very tight and accurate without taking  over the mids and the high frequencies  are very clear in fact with some tracks  like rock songs the high notes can  actually be a little bit too sharp if  the volume is maxed out but for that we  found not turning down the volume just  one notch on the iPhone which is about  seven percent or so really helps but  with most tracks especially those worth  heavy vocals and high notes like  electronics these sound very good  of course sound is subjective but what  is this objective is that these beats  sound way more balanced than any  previous Beats headphones that I've  listened to and in a few songs that I  really like I noticed some of the sound  effects some of the electronic effects  that were kind of subdued with my other  headphones and blended into the mids  whereas because of the really good  high-frequency clarity those really  start to stand out now let's get into  noise cancellation and this was our  final surprise with these headphones  everybody knows that these Sony's are  top-of-the-line but honestly we didn't  hear that much of a difference between  them our office is located right next  door to their furnace room so we have a  constant low-frequency droning noise and  these get rid of them completely just  like the Sony's I didn't get a chance to  fly with them so we don't know how they  would compare to the Sony's in that  location but in normal use they are  shockingly close we thought that for  most people the noise cancellation of  the air pod pros are more than good  enough and the beats solo pros are  definitely better with low-end and  dramatically better with high frequency  sounds so we think that for the large  majority of people they will be very  happy with the beats solo pros another  major feature is the ambient mode which  uses the mics to let you hear your  environment and just like the previously  mentioned ear pods this feature sounds  much more natural than other brands that  we have tested  which tend to sound digital battery life  is great with about 20 hours of use with  either noise cancellation or am memo  turned on or about 40 hours with it off  in 10 minutes of fast charging gives you  about 3 hours of use I need to be  completely honest with you guys  I kind of came into this review a bit  biased against Beats headphones but  trying them out for the first time and  then for a few days after that I am way  more impressed and I like these way more  than I expected and after using them  overall I would highly recommend them if  you're looking for a pair of on your  headphones that are premium at that  price point and you want that really  nice noise cancellation overall the  whole package really makes sense if you  can afford them and the sound quality is  really good thank you guys for watching  if you want to see my comparison against  the Sony's  you guys can check that out right over  there and click above to subscribe and  down below to enable notifications this  has been max with Max tech and I will  see you in the next video  [Music]
 

